## No Python interop

This workspace is pure Rust: no pyo3, no embedded interpreter, no extension module, nothing that
imports a Python package. `pyproject.toml` exists for the dev tooling alone: the `ruff`, `ty`,
and `pytest` that `mise` runs over the toolchain helpers in `scripts/`.

Logic lives in `crates/core`, written against traits, so it compiles and tests on its own and an
implementation can be swapped without touching callers.
{% if cookiecutter.crate_type != 'lib' %}
`crates/cli` is a thin binary over that core; logic does not live there.
{% endif %}
